  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "How many fighter jets must be allocated exclusively for pilot training each year — is this a fixed number, a fraction of that year's production, or a fraction of the total fleet available at the start of the year?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy definition regarding the allocation method for training jets, presenting mutually exclusive options for one specific parameter."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 2,
  "is_atomic": false,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What fraction of each year's production must be allocated to pilot training — is it the same fraction in both years?",
    "What is its value?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks whether the fraction is the same in both years (a yes/no or policy question) and separately asks for the specific value of that fraction. These are two semantically independent requests because the user could confirm the fraction is the same without providing the number, or provide the number without explicitly confirming uniformity."
}

